Design an In-Memory File System. ->
Design an object-oriented file system that exists in memory. The system should support the following operations:
ls(String path): Given a path, if it is a file path, return a list containing just the file's name.
If it is a directory path, return a list of all files and directory names in that directory. The output should be sorted lexicographically.
mkdir(String path): Create a new directory according to the given path. If the intermediate directories in the path do not exist, create them as well.
addContentToFile(String filePath, String content): Given a file path and file content in string format, append the content to the existing file.
If the file does not exist, create a new file containing the given content.
readContentFromFile(String filePath): Given a file path, return its string content.

